# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-10-25 after a coverage check against the class material (Day 5
# deck, Vulnerability & Penetration Testing transcript) and build/cysa-spine.json:
# objective 2.2 names specific tools and the drill named none of them; 2.1 was
# missing the ICS components and ping sweeps. Original prose.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

FLASHCARDS += [
 ('2.2', 'Match each tool to its job: Nmap, Angry IP Scanner, Maltego, Recon-ng.',
  'Nmap: host discovery, port scanning, service and OS detection, plus scripted checks.\nAngry IP Scanner: a fast, lightweight GUI sweep of an address range for live hosts and open ports.\nMaltego: OSINT link analysis, graphing how domains, people, email addresses and infrastructure connect.\nRecon-ng: a modular command-line OSINT framework that harvests hosts, contacts and credentials from public sources.'),
 ('2.2', 'What do these Nmap options do: -sn, -sS, -sV, -O, -sU, -p-?',
  '-sn: host discovery only, no port scan.\n-sS: TCP SYN ("half-open") scan, the default when run with privileges.\n-sV: probe open ports to identify service and version.\n-O: operating system fingerprinting.\n-sU: UDP scan, slow but the only way to see services like SNMP and DNS.\n-p-: all 65,535 ports instead of the top 1,000.'),
 ('2.2', 'Nmap reports a port as open, closed or filtered. What does each mean?',
  'Open: a service answered. Closed: the host answered that nothing listens there, so the host is up and reachable. Filtered: no answer at all, usually because a firewall dropped the probe, so Nmap cannot tell whether a service exists. Filtered is a statement about the path, not the port.'),
 ('2.2', 'Nessus and OpenVAS: what are they, and how do they differ?',
  'Both are network vulnerability scanners that run thousands of plugin checks against hosts and report findings with a severity, CVSS score, evidence and a solution. Nessus is Tenable\'s commercial product; OpenVAS is the open-source scanner maintained by Greenbone. Functionally they answer the same question.'),
 ('2.2', 'Which parts of a Nessus or OpenVAS finding should you read before acting on it?',
  'The plugin output (the actual evidence the scanner saw, such as a banner or a file version), how it was detected (remote banner versus credentialed check), the affected port, and the solution. Severity alone tells you nothing about whether the finding is real on this host.'),
 ('2.2', 'Burp Suite: what is it, and what is it used for?',
  'An intercepting web proxy that sits between the browser and the application, so a tester can capture, read and modify every request. Repeater resends edited requests, Intruder automates payloads against parameters, and the Professional edition adds an automated scanner. It is the standard tool for manual web application testing.'),
 ('2.2', 'How does OWASP ZAP compare with Burp Suite?',
  'ZAP (Zed Attack Proxy) is the free, open-source equivalent: an intercepting proxy with a spider and an automated active scanner. Its scriptable API and headless mode make it a common choice for scanning inside a CI/CD pipeline.'),
 ('2.2', 'Nikto and Arachni: what kind of tools are they?',
  'Both are web scanners. Nikto is a command-line web server scanner that checks for outdated server software, dangerous default files and misconfigurations; it is fast and very noisy. Arachni is an automated web application scanning framework that crawls an application and tests for flaws such as XSS and SQL injection. Arachni is no longer actively developed but remains on the objective list.'),
 ('2.2', 'What is Metasploit used for in vulnerability work?',
  'Validating exploitability. It is an exploitation framework of modules: exploits, payloads and auxiliary scanners. You set the target (RHOSTS), the payload and the listener (LHOST), then run it. A scanner says a flaw might exist; a successful Metasploit module shows that it does.'),
 ('2.2', 'GDB versus Immunity Debugger.',
  'Both are debuggers for examining a program as it runs: registers, memory and control flow. GDB is the GNU command-line debugger used mainly on Linux. Immunity Debugger is a Windows GUI debugger with Python scripting, long used for exploit development. Pick by platform.'),
 ('2.2', 'Scout Suite, Prowler and Pacu are all cloud tools. What separates them?',
  'Scout Suite audits the configuration of AWS, Azure and GCP accounts through their APIs and produces a report of risky settings. Prowler runs security best-practice and CIS benchmark checks, mainly for AWS. Pacu is offensive: an AWS exploitation framework that tests what an attacker could do with a set of compromised credentials. The first two assess posture; Pacu attacks it.'),
 ('2.2', 'Which tool would you reach for to: find live hosts, find host vulnerabilities, test a web login form, prove a flaw is exploitable, review cloud permissions?',
  'Live hosts: Nmap or Angry IP Scanner.\nHost vulnerabilities: Nessus or OpenVAS.\nWeb login form: Burp Suite or ZAP.\nProve exploitability: Metasploit.\nCloud permissions: Scout Suite or Prowler (Pacu if the test is offensive).'),
 ('2.1', 'In an industrial control system, what do a PLC, an RTU and an HMI each do?',
  'A PLC (programmable logic controller) runs the control logic for local equipment in real time. An RTU (remote terminal unit) gathers telemetry from distant field sites and relays it to the SCADA master. An HMI (human-machine interface) is the operator\'s screen for watching and controlling the process.'),
 ('2.1', 'Why are HMIs and engineering workstations high-value targets?',
  'They usually run ordinary Windows, they are often reachable from the IT network, and they can issue commands to the physical process. That makes them the most common bridge from a compromised office network into operational technology.'),
 ('2.1', 'What is a ping sweep, and what are its limits?',
  'Sending ICMP echo requests across an address range to see which hosts answer: the quickest form of host discovery. Hosts that block ICMP look absent, so TCP, UDP or ARP discovery is used alongside it. On OT networks even a sweep should be cleared first.'),
]

QUIZ += [
 ('2.2', 'An external Nmap scan reports 3389/tcp as filtered. What can you conclude?',
  ['RDP is running and exposed to the internet', 'Something in the path dropped the probe, so the port\'s real state is unknown', 'The host is down', 'RDP is installed but disabled'],
  1, 'Filtered means no response came back, which is what a firewall silently dropping packets produces. It is not evidence that a service exists or that it does not. Closed would mean the host answered that nothing is listening.'),
 ('2.2', 'You need to audit an AWS account\'s configuration against CIS benchmarks without changing anything. Which tool fits?',
  ['Pacu', 'Prowler', 'Metasploit', 'Burp Suite'],
  1, 'Prowler runs read-only best-practice and CIS checks against AWS. Pacu is an exploitation framework for attacking AWS with compromised credentials, Metasploit targets hosts and services, and Burp Suite targets web applications.'),
 ('2.2', 'A penetration tester holds leaked AWS access keys and wants to test which privilege-escalation paths they open. Which tool is built for this?',
  ['Scout Suite', 'Pacu', 'Nessus', 'Maltego'],
  1, 'Pacu is an offensive AWS framework with modules for enumerating permissions and escalating privileges from a set of credentials. Scout Suite reports on configuration but does not attack it.'),
 ('2.2', 'You need to capture a login request, change a parameter and resend it to see how the application responds. Which tool?',
  ['Nikto', 'Burp Suite', 'OpenVAS', 'Angry IP Scanner'],
  1, 'Intercepting, editing and replaying requests is exactly what an intercepting proxy does; Burp Suite (or ZAP) is the tool. Nikto and OpenVAS run automated checks and do not let you hand-edit traffic.'),
 ('2.2', 'Which tool maps relationships between an organization\'s domains, email addresses and employees from public sources?',
  ['Maltego', 'Nmap', 'GDB', 'Prowler'],
  0, 'Maltego is OSINT link analysis: it pulls public data and draws the connections between entities as a graph. That is reconnaissance, not vulnerability scanning.'),
 ('2.2', 'A Nessus finding says Apache is vulnerable, detected from the version in the server banner. The host is a distribution that backports security fixes. What should you do first?',
  ['Patch Apache immediately', 'Verify the installed package version with a credentialed check before acting', 'Close the finding as a false positive', 'Raise the severity because the banner is exposed'],
  1, 'Distributions often fix a flaw without changing the upstream version number, so a banner-only detection can be a false positive. Reading the actual package version settles it. Closing it without checking is as wrong as patching blindly.'),
 ('2.2', 'A scanner reports a remote code execution flaw on a test server, and you need to show the change board it is real. Which tool demonstrates that?',
  ['Metasploit', 'Recon-ng', 'Angry IP Scanner', 'Scout Suite'],
  0, 'Running a matching Metasploit module against a test system turns "the scanner thinks so" into a demonstrated exploit, which is what changes priority. Do it only with authorization and only in a controlled environment.'),
 ('2.2', 'You are debugging a crashing Windows service and want a GUI debugger you can script in Python. Which one?',
  ['GDB', 'Immunity Debugger', 'Nikto', 'ZAP'],
  1, 'Immunity Debugger is a Windows GUI debugger with Python scripting. GDB is the GNU command-line debugger used mostly on Linux. The other two are web scanners.'),
 ('2.1', 'Which ICS component collects data from distant field sites, such as pipeline pumping stations, and reports it to the SCADA master?',
  ['PLC', 'RTU', 'HMI', 'Historian'],
  1, 'Remote terminal units sit at geographically spread sites and relay telemetry to the central SCADA system. PLCs run local control logic, the HMI is the operator\'s display, and a historian stores process data over time.'),
]

